<article class="env-lemma" id="05ZP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05ZP">Lemma <span data-tag="05ZP">76.9.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X \subset X'$ be a thickening of algebraic spaces over $S$. For any open subspace $U \subset X$ there exists a unique open subspace $U' \subset X'$ such that $U = X \times _{X'} U'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $U' \to X'$ be the object of $X'_{spaces, {\acute{e}tale}}$ corresponding to the object $U \to X$ of $X_{spaces, {\acute{e}tale}}$ via (<a href="/tag/05ZL" data-tag="05ZL">76.9.1.1</a>). The morphism $U' \to X'$ is étale and universally injective, hence an open immersion, see Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/05W5" data-tag="05W5">67.51.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>